I go into the sports hall to the reception desk.
A staff member stands there and greets me.
"Good evening, how can I help you?" he asks.
"Good evening," I answer.
"I want to participate as a guest today."
The staff member nods.
"Gladly."
"That costs seven euros," he says.
"But I do not have a racket," I explain.
"Can I rent a racket?"
"Yes, of course," he replies.
"The racket costs three euros."
That makes ten euros in total.
I open my backpack and take my money.
I pay with a ten-euro note.
He takes the money and prints the receipt.
"Do you want the receipt?" he asks.
"No, thank you," I reply.
He gives me the racket.
"Have fun!" he says.
